From 6e4ff477f9e04416da08ebbf45cc7c4acbd264f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agent OS <agent-os@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 02:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 23/31] Input: misc: add OnePlus 3 S1302 capacitive keys

The OnePlus 3 has a separate Synaptics S1302 controller for the two
capacitive chin keys.  Its interrupt is on TLMM GPIO 132 and its key state
register is on RMI page 2, register 0.  The existing mainline RMI4 driver
does not implement the legacy S1302 key function, so expose the two keys as
a normal EV_KEY input device.

The driver deliberately reports only the physical left/recent key and right
back key.  The center fingerprint/home button is a separate device and is
not part of this controller.

Signed-off-by: Agent OS <agent-os@example.invalid>
---
 .../bindings/input/oneplus,s1302-capkey.yaml  |  42 ++++
 drivers/input/misc/Kconfig                    |  11 +
 drivers/input/misc/Makefile                   |   1 +
 drivers/input/misc/op3-capkey-s1302.c         | 201 ++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 255 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/oneplus,s1302-capkey.yaml
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/misc/op3-capkey-s1302.c

